# rm256, the hollow tread (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm256
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_gerrit_ropewick
written_by codex
title the hollow tread
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk taps_each_landing_to_hear_the_hollow
likes roast_pork swimming tidy_house first_snow
dislikes drizzle rats
fears unseated_stones a_landing_giving_way
hopes a_smooth_swimming_ledge geese_far_from_the_roast
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.5 land +0.3 home +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=dry tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# trots up a flight with apparent ease, taps the landing before putting weight on it, and keeps a dry remark ready for the breathless.

words
oath! = Soft mortar take it | Hollowest stone below
saying! = Trust the landing after the knock | A step can lie quite level
knock = a knuckle tap | a tap with my heel
slab = the landing stone | the broad flag
hollow = a drum note | a hollow knock
rubble = odds of broken stone | a heap of sharp chips
floatwood = my bit of driftwood | a bleached stick
joint = the narrow joint | that seam in the flags
dipper = a tin scoop | the little water scoop
crispbit = the crackling end | a corner of crisp skin
wake = the crease behind a swimmer | a line in quiet water
broomtip = the blunt broom end | my short brush handle
highrock = the dry rock | the flat bank stone
neatrow = a row of tidy toes | shoes lined up in pairs

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A House can afford stairs with a roof over them. Winter would too if somebody sent it the bill.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A meal lent me strength once. I never found where to pay it back except into the very same pot.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I've yet to see the scales tipped by what's left in a buyer's purse.
opinion @1 sump for 2 : On a steep lane folk learn to pass a heavy thing along without being asked to love the carrier.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : Good flags last longer than praise. I'd pay for the first and save my breath on the second.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A seat when you're tired is worth a whole sermon about rest.

grown
line @1 greet : Come up level with me. No prize for arriving winded. | Here, a level bit to speak on.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New tread. Welcome all the same.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Dawn's only halfway up the hill. We can wait for it.
line @1 greet.return : Hullo across the gap. | I heard your greeting over my footfall.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Step where you heard me, there's room.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're allowed to laugh if I miss a step. Blood privilege.
line @1 again.open : Our feet seem to have planned this without us.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Up on the level, over here!
line @1 farewell : A sound step under you. | Don't let the hill hurry you downward.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll hear you coming back, I expect.
line @1 react.news.new : That's come up the hill ahead of my ears for once.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard that account already. The echo's very fair.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd put a little weight on that before I trusted the story.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Miserable news. There's room to sit if it's taken your legs.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Well, there's a landing worth stopping on.
line @1 answer.how : Sound at the corners, given a quiet tap.
line @1 ask.how : How much hill have you left in you today?
line @1 sympathise : It was a bad step. No sense pretending it didn't hurt.
line @1 decline : I'd sooner decline now than set you down halfway up.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. My legs can carry my own errand.
line @1 thank : You've given my knees a reprieve.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Don't waste breath. There's still a bit of climb.
line @1 preclose : Best finish this flight before I stiffen.
line @1 accept_preclose : Away when you're ready. I can lean quite comfortably here.
line @1 ack : Ah. Solid enough.
scene landing
when topic=land|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That landing answers twice if you give it #knock#. | I try each flat step before I rest on it.
b : Twice? I heard one sound. | Aren't the flat ones safest?
a : One from the face, then the loose corner talks back. | Flat's what the top looks like. The bottom gets a vote.

scene carry
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=laborer
does offer / accept / assess
a : Give me the lower end on the ascent. | Let me take that bundle beside the wall.
b : Glad to. You'll have the weight. | That's a squeeze. Why that side?
a : You'll have to walk backwards. I'd sooner take the weight. | So if I bump something it's a wall and hasn't got feelings.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / give.advice / concede
a : This little fine rain gets in behind each ear. | I could forgive the wet if it made up its mind to fall.
b : Turn your collar up. | Have a run, then you'll know it's wet.
a : Then both ears are deaf and damp. Still, one improvement. | A run costs breakfast. I'll settle for walking and complaining.

scene swims
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I float a stick ahead before I go in. | I never swim directly towards the towel.
b : To see how cold the water is? | Worried somebody's moved it?
a : Stick wouldn't tell me cold. The stick does tell me where I'm going. | Because by the time I arrive where it was I'll be passing it.

scene rind
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The crisp edge goes last on my plate. | Hear that snap? That's the bit worth chewing slowly.
b : Doesn't it get cold? | Which snap?
a : Precisely. Hot fat would only hurry me. | The second. First was my jaw getting ready.

scene wintersteps
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like an untouched fall, except where there's a stair underneath. | Snow makes a fine white line over the crack by a door.
b : Can't you count the steps? | Why's that fine?
a : Steps I can count. The bit somebody knocked out I can't. | Left to myself I'd never notice the draft that drew the line.

scene broom
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does give.opinion / challenge / concede
a : A broom's best kept on a nail, clear of the floor. | I put shoes toe out after I sweep.
b : You're fussy about a broom. | What about muddy toes?
a : It's allowed one fault. Most of us have two. | Good point. Toe out on a sack is the civil arrangement.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rat went about my loaf in a remarkably tidy manner. | I can endure rats until one starts looking comfortable.
b : Crumbs all in a heap? | How would you know?
a : Not a crumb. Just room where the loaf had been. | It turns its back while eating. Insult on top of expense.

scene quiet
when topic=gossip
does confide / react.self / assess
a : There are things seen through an open door that belong inside it. | I find I hear less gossip if I carry something heavy.
b : You're good at closing doors, then. | Nobody likes to interrupt work?
a : I'm better at finding something else to look at. | It's that I can't spare the breath to pass it on.

scene shore
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The headland path gives you a view of the whole wall sideways. | From outside the walls the climbs look rather grand.
b : Sideways is better? | And from inside?
a : You see the thickness. From inside you see which footsore soul is climbing it. | From inside they're measures of breakfast spent.

scene wages
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could pay with blisters if anybody gave change for them. | When money runs close I count things that aren't coins.
b : What sort of change? | What things?
a : Soft socks, mostly. Rare currency on this hill. | Meals left, journeys owed, and the friendliest door on the route.

scene my_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take the long climb to spend ten quiet minutes with #self.friend#. | I could walk in silence quite happily beside #self.friend#.
b : Is ten minutes worth all that labour? | But what makes you call it a good visit?
a : A fine excuse to get my breath back. I'd stay twenty. | By how far I've gone without wondering when I might turn back.

scene tool
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Never fill a hod up to the rim on your first lift. | Those little chips go under #slab# to stop a rock.
b : Saving some for next time? | Any old chip?
a : Saving my shoulders for the last lift. Same shoulders all day. | Try it first. A rocking chip only gives the slab a partner.

scene chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a hymn I can keep pace to. | If I miss a word of prayer, I let the gap stay put.
b : While climbing? | Doesn't that bother you?
a : Coming down. Going up I leave the long notes to fitter wolves. | I doubt the Bright One's waiting with a slate to mark the stumble.

scene walkback
when topic=travel|day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I hear someone running downhill I step aside first and look after. | Down a slope my two paws seem to have different ideas.
b : You expect a collision? | One wants to go faster?
a : I expect a runner. Collisions happen after expectations. | The left wants a low wall to sit on. The right's coming round to it.

scene sleeper
when topic=health
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : My knees sometimes make a noise I wish the stairs would own. | A long rest makes getting up rather public.
b : Both knees at once? | The grunt gives you away.
a : One calls and one answers. Good neighbours, if noisy. | I cough just beforehand. Leave the audience some uncertainty.

scene bad_road
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : With the wagon overdue, I'll enjoy sitting on the lower landing. | No wagon yet. I can hear each loose wheel on each little barrow.
b : Till it arrives, anyway. | How many loose wheels?
a : That's the nature of a holiday. Use the narrow ones too. | Seven by sound, though one may be doing steady business going round.

scene night_top
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The dark makes a short stair one step longer in my head. | I like returning by a wall at night. It keeps the same side.
b : How can you spot the real end? | Streets don't move either.
a : I set one foot down carefully on a step that isn't there. Familiar little surprise. | No, but I do. A small correction never hurt a tired walker.

story double_run [topic=memories self.age>=20]
  : As a pup I tried to take a whole stair in three grand bounds.
  : Two got me there. The third took me straight through somebody's basket of washing.
  b : Did you catch it before it scattered?
  : I brought the washing back up one careful step at a time. Learned two gaits that day.

story riverstick [topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming]
  : I threw a stick ahead on my first long swim and set my sights on overtaking it.
  : It stuck in a clump of grass and I went sailing by, triumphant.
  b : Hardly a race if the stick's stuck.
  : My greatest triumph. I've been very selective about my rivals ever since.

story missing_square [topic=home self.likes=tidy_house]
  : I swept a tidy square for my boots and stood back to inspect it.
  : There was a perfect print dead centre on the square.
  b : Whose print?
  : Mine. I had two excellent suspects right under my nose, but I inspected each sole in the room.

rule @load
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the bottom corner room to swing! | Mind those chips under the load.

rule @stairs
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let somebody coming down have the outside edge. | Weight well inside the landing edge!

rule @frost
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear the lip as well as the tread. | Snow hasn't made those steps any broader.

rule @brush
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Boots in pairs by the low board! | Hang the brush where its toes can dry.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Take the flat spot beside me. We've no need to do this on a slope.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : More climbing for you, #topic.player#? I'll lean here while you tell me.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Dark enough to go by voice. What brings you up?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Make the case from your own side of the tread.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : At #self.workplace# I carry from the high stack to the low one, or the reverse when someone's measured wrong.
dlg @2 resident.job : My test of good work is whether a thing stays put after I've let go.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Up from below comes this word. #world.news.capitalize#. See if it stands.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Go easily. The steps will keep their own count.
graft resident.hub
choice What were you tapping for? -> landing_echo
node landing_echo
say Two edges of a flag should give one note. If the corners disagree I put my weight elsewhere.
choice Could you do it by foot? -> heel_echo
choice Look at something else. -> hub
node heel_echo
say One heel, laid down easy. Jump on it and you'll learn the answer far quicker than you wanted.
choice I'll mind the corners. -> hub
choice Go on up. -> bye
